WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:08.240
On the political stage, he can be magnetic.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:13.959
Much like he is when performing his music
for fans.

00:00:13.959 --> 00:00:17.869
But Bobi Wine says his entertainment career
is being curtailed.

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:20.000
"I just wonder why the police continue to
persecute me.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.850
More than fifteen of my concerts have been
cancelled.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:32.250
The promoters of my music have been told to
stop working with me so that they can be allowed

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.450
to work."

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.960
On December 15th, Bobi Wine tweeted that police
had attempted to block him from performing

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.110
a show in the town of Jinja.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.940
He managed to escape arrest and later gave
his account of what happened to DW:

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.860
“It was 8 O’clock in the night when the
Police raided the hotel when the army started

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:58.910
beating and arresting people.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:05.180
Some kind people helped me to elude them and
I disappeared from that place and they looked

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:10.650
for me the entire night but they could not
see me"

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:16.540
Bobi Wine believes the police don't want him
performing his music shows as he is using

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:22.530
them as an opportunity to make political statements.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:28.340
When the government was asked to respond to
the claims, Uganda's security minister answered

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.460
in parliament.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:42.890
“I asked him (Bobi Wine) a question, how
will you balance your music with politics?

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:53.820
I will say that these are occupational hazards."

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:59.770
Bobi Wine won a seat in the Ugandan parliament
in 2017.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:05.820
This followed more than 15 successful years
as a musician, a career he has refused to

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.870
give up.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:15.460
"I am going to continue singing my music and
I am going to continue organizing my concerts.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:22.070
When the Police continuously blocks me from
practicing my profession, from feeding my

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.440
family, they are continuously exposing themselves"

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:32.970
In August, Bobi Wine was arrested at a political
rally and reportedly tortured.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:36.940
He was later charged with treason.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:42.660
Bobi Wine has been a fierce critic of President
Yoweri Museveni, who's been in power for more

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.870
than 30 years.

